###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The test sets mix high- and low-entropy oxides; results are attached to the high-entropy material and the labels say 'HE and LE oxides'. Separate HE/LE errors are not stated.
# - Final training and validation losses (0.0732, 0.0734) are unitless loss values and are not encoded. The pre-trained model's fitted-line intercept (-1.456 eV/atom) and slope (0.715) are not error metrics.
# - MC conformation search, Na interaction energies, ionic/cationic potentials and conformational entropies (Table 1) are property analyses.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/wu2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

